{% from "components/nav-item.njk" import navItem %}
{% from "components/icon.njk" import icon %}
{#
  SITE FOOTER — Figma 568:39273 (desktop 275:57838, mobile 568:39274).

  WHAT THIS ITERATION REPLACED. The right half used to be three link columns —
  Case studies from collections.workCards, More works, Get in touch — and the
  left half was the sign-off with the copyright pushed to the bottom of a
  stretched column. The node keeps the left half's content and drops all three
  columns, so the whole right half is now one illustration and the left half
  grows two rows of its own: the Email Me / Set a Meeting actions and the
  "Find me on" chips. site.js lost footer.titles and footer.moreWorks with them.

  WHAT DID NOT MOVE, because the node measures the same as the one this was
  built to: the 120px page margin, the two gutter rules on the inner container,
  its 32px inset and 120px block padding, the heading and tagline strings, and
  the copyright's two spans bottom-left. That is the whole reason this is a
  content change rather than a reframe.

  #contact AND data-header-theme STAY ON THIS ELEMENT. The id is what every
  "Contact" link in the header points at and what header-theme.js observes for
  the nav's selected state; the theme flag is what inverts the header as it
  passes over this band. Neither is affected by anything below them, but both
  are easy to drop by accident when a section is rebuilt, so: they are load
  bearing, leave them.

  THE COPYRIGHT IS NO LONGER PUSHED. It used to be positioned by
  justify-content:space-between against the height of the tallest link column;
  with the columns gone there is nothing to push against, so the comp's own
  80px sits under the chips instead. See _footer.css.

  THE ACTIONS KEEP navItem(), the chips do not. The two text links are the same
  Figma Nav_item component the header uses (410:66301) and roll on hover like
  every other one; the chips are glyphs with no text to roll, so they take their
  accessible name from the link's aria-label and the icon stays decorative.

  THE MONOGRAM IS aria-hidden AND OUTSIDE THE READING ORDER. It carries no
  meaning the copyright line does not already state, and it is the last thing in
  the DOM so a screen reader reaches the sign-off, the links and the copyright
  in that order regardless of where it sits visually.
#}

<footer class="site-footer" id="contact" data-header-theme="dark">
  <div class="site-footer__inner">
    <div class="site-footer__row">

      <div class="site-footer__intro">

        {# Sign-off and the two actions: one group, because the comp sets 24px
           between them and 80px to everything below. #}
        <div class="site-footer__contact">
          <div class="site-footer__intro-text">
            <h2 class="site-footer__heading">{{ site.footer.heading }}</h2>
            <p class="site-footer__tagline">{{ site.footer.tagline }}</p>
          </div>

          <ul class="site-footer__actions">
            {%- for a in site.footer.actions %}
              <li>
                <a
                  class="site-footer__action"
                  href="{{ a.url }}"
                  {%- if a.external %} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"{% endif %}
                >{{ navItem(a.name) }}</a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="site-footer__social">
          <h3 class="site-footer__social-title">{{ site.footer.socialTitle }}</h3>
          <ul class="site-footer__chips">
            {%- for s in site.footer.socials %}
              <li>
                <a
                  class="site-footer__chip"
                  href="{{ s.url }}"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  aria-label="{{ s.name }}"
                >{{ icon(s.icon, size=28) }}</a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="site-footer__copyright">
          <span>&copy; {{ site.copyrightYear }},</span>
          <span>{{ site.footer.siteName }}</span>
        </p>
      </div>

      {# THE VIEWBOX IS THE GLYPH'S MEASURED BOUNDS, not the wordmark's 40-unit
         grid — see the note on icon.njk's `box` argument. Measured with
         getBBox() on the three paths: x 8.376..32.064, y 2.635..37.364. #}
      <div class="site-footer__mark" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ icon("logo-mark", box="8.376 2.635 23.688 34.728") }}
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
